[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5486702738","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123048#issuecomment-5486702738","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123048","id":5486702738,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRwhwkg","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-01T00:27:57Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T00:27:57Z","body":"Nice find. I spent at least a week trying to get Godot Rapier Physics 3D joints to match Godot and confronted some pretty weird stuff.\n\nI believe that the issue here is that the cone joint widget is drawn incorrectly. \n\nThe actual cone joint always twists around its X axis. So if you align that connecting rod along the x axis, things should start to make sense.\n\nThe widget seems to just draw one cone from the joint position toward body A, and then another cone from the joint position to body B.\n\n<img width=\"557\" height=\"452\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eacf07f1-bcef-41a2-9885-962f3d29af94\" />\n\n*this joint widget (above) is incorrect and misleading, and those cones aren't equal and opposite, and not down the joint x axis.*\n\nI think the widget should show two equal and opposite cones down the x axis of the joint in the editor. I also think the documentation is a bit challenging, but I am not certain I could describe it better. It's a difficult joint.\n\nSo I believe that the fix to this issue is to fix the ConeTwistJoint3D editor widget.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5486702738/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5489401630","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123048#issuecomment-5489401630","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123048","id":5489401630,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRzGfHg","user":{"login":"EdwardChanCH","id":97891482,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdW0mg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97891482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH","html_url":"https://github.com/EdwardChanCH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-01T05:35:25Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T05:35:25Z","body":"> I believe that the issue here is that the cone joint widget is drawn incorrectly.\n\nAh, I opened this issue expecting `ConeTwiseJoint3D` to be set up based on the origin/ center of mass of the two bodies. Since the x-axis behaviour is intended, maybe better documentation of `swing_span` and `twist_span` is enough to close this issue.\n\nThe editor widget bug is tracked in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/40885.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5489401630/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5502396054","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123048#issuecomment-5502396054","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123048","id":5502396054,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABR_fmlg","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-02T00:16:50Z","updated_at":"2026-09-02T00:18:42Z","body":"Of course, the widget being wrong doesn't explain the joint losing it's anchoring so easily in your second video :/","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5502396054/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]